3. Smart Contract

3.1 Purpose

The smart contract defines rules for the savings pool:

Deposits can be made by anyone at any time

Only the pool owner can withdraw funds

Withdrawals allowed only after a deadline


This ensures trustless saving with enforced rules.


---

3.2 Code Explanation

The Plutus contract SavingsPool.hs defines:

A custom Action data type

A validator that checks whether a transaction is a Deposit or Withdraw

For Withdraw, no logic is currently enforced (can be extended)


Critical validator logic:

{-# INLINABLE mkValidator #-}
mkValidator :: BuiltinData -> BuiltinData -> BuiltinData -> ()
mkValidator _ redeemer _ =
    case PlutusTx.unsafeFromBuiltinData @Action redeemer of
        Deposit  -> ()
        Withdraw -> ()

This snippet shows stub logic — extendable with owner checks and deadlines.


---

3.3 Usage

To use the contract:

1. Compile with Plutus tools


2. Lock ADA in the contract by submitting a transaction with Deposit


3. Owner can unlock ADA with Withdraw after conditions are met




